<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate fell in this week's primary auction and demand rose, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	23.06	    - 22	    22.94     23.25</p>
<p>91-Day	25.63	    -112	    25.50     25.75</p>
<p>182-Day     27.33	    - 83	    27.00     27.43</p>
<p>364-Day     27.39				27.23     27.46</p>
<p>Last week the 343-day paper was assigned at 28.03 pct.</p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	900 million pesos   3.26 bln pesos     3.62</p>
<p>91-Day	900 million pesos   5.76 bln pesos     6.40</p>
<p>182-Day     900 million pesos   4.81 bln pesos     5.34</p>
<p>364-Day     600 million pesos   3.62 bln pesos     6.03</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 5.28 compared with 4.69 the week before, on demand of 15.48 billion pesos the week before.</p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			   19   basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			   12   basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			  10   basis points</p>
<p>    364-Day			   7   basis points</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom, 525 728-9559. E-mail at robert.kozak@reuters.com</p>
</text>
